// =============================================================================
// Service surface: requests, responses, supporting messages
// =============================================================================
//
// All RPCs are unary except where noted. Map keys for denormalized results
// are the canonical string form of an Id: `"<namespace>/<slug>@<version>"`.
// Tools must not parse this key -- it is opaque routing data. Use the
// returned Entity.id (or the embedded EntityRef) for any semantic decision.
//
// ---------- Branch context (Phase 1: Isolation) ------------------------------
//
// A branch is a small server-side overlay of copy-on-write deltas over the
// baseline store (see docs/explanation/branching.md). Branch context is NOT
// a field on any request message below. Every RPC except CreateBranch /
// ListBranches / DeleteBranch resolves an optional branch from the gRPC
// metadata header `x-trogon-atlas-branch` (a plain string, not base64/bin).
// When absent, the RPC operates against baseline exactly as before this
// header existed.
//
// SearchEntities and DeleteByQuery are included in that rule. Both were
// carved out when branching first landed -- search because the tantivy
// index is built over baseline, DeleteByQuery because a full-store sweep
// has no obvious branch semantics -- and both carve-outs are gone: search
// under a branch queries a per-branch index over the merged view, and a
// sweep lands its deletes as branch deltas. The registry RPCs
// (RegisterNamespace, MoveNamespace) read and write the namespace registry,
// which is not copy-on-write, so the header changes nothing there.
//
// Branch names follow the same charset as an id component
// (`trogon_atlas_core::validate_id_component`: ASCII alphanumeric, '-', '_',
// '.', max 200 chars per segment, no leading '.'), with at most one '/'
// separator allowed to express an owner prefix, e.g. "alex/retention-rework".

